#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197948 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "9a1112c0-db94-5572-ba53-b78116b7c273" :question/math-academy-id "e-12355" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r(u,v)$, where\n\n$\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) =\\left\\langle x+y,\\: x-y,\\: xyz \\right\\rangle, \\quad \\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u^2,\\: v^2,\\: 1 \\right\\rangle, \\quad (u,v)\\in D\\subset \\mathbb{R}^2$.\n\nIf the flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $S$ with respect to $\\mathbf{n}$ is given by\n\n$AAAAAAA$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D$, the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S} = \\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S = \\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(v^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2u, 0, 0⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(v^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 2v, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 0, 4uv⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(r(u, v)) &= ⟨x + y, x - y, xyz⟩ \\mid _{x = u^{2}y = v^{2}z = 1} \\\\\n&= ⟨u^{2} + v^{2}, u^{2} - v^{2}, u^{2}v^{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(r(u, v)) \\cdot (r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′}) &= ⟨u^{2} + v^{2}, u^{2} - v^{2}, u^{2}v^{2}⟩ \\cdot ⟨0, 0, 4uv⟩ \\\\\n&= (u^{2} + v^{2}) \\cdot 0 + (u^{2} - v^{2}) \\cdot 0 + u^{2}v^{2} \\cdot 4uv \\\\\n&= 4u^{3}v^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(S)F \\cdot dS &= ∬_(D)F(r(u, v)) \\cdot (r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′})dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)4 u 3 v 3dA\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197950 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "0364a11f-e567-517e-acf2-471708dbdc0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12358" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n$\\iint\\limits_S \\left\\langle z, \\: x, \\: y \\right\\rangle \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle 1+2u+v, \\: u+v, \\: u-v \\right\\rangle$\n\nfor $0 \\leq u \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 1$." :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D$, the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S} = \\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S = \\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1 + 2u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2, 1, 1⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1 + 2u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 1,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 2, 3, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(r(u, v)) &= ⟨z, x, y⟩ \\mid _{x = 1 + 2u + vy = u + vz = u - v} \\\\\n&= ⟨u - v, 1 + 2u + v, u + v⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(r(u, v)) \\cdot (r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′}) &= ⟨u - v, 1 + 2u + v, u + v⟩ \\cdot ⟨ - 2, 3, 1⟩ \\\\\n&= (u - v) \\cdot (-2) + (1 + 2u + v) \\cdot 3 + (u + v) \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&=-2u + 2v + 3 + 6u + 3v + u + v \\\\\n&= 5u + 6v + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(S)⟨z, x, y⟩ \\cdot dS &= ∬_(D)F(r(u, v)) \\cdot (r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′})dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)(5u + 6v + 3)dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{1}(5u + 6v + 3)dvdu \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}[5uv + 3v^{2} + 3v]_{v = 0}^{v = 1}du \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}(5u + 6)du \\\\\n&= [\\frac{5}{2}u^{2} + 6u]_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= 10 + 12 \\\\\n&= 22\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "888ad587-c5a4-5a4a-b25e-23442b9f6145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4uv^{3} + 2u^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193974} {:answer/id #uuid "12cb63f6-04da-555f-b2ff-3767b04d83b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193975} {:answer/id #uuid "36224e2f-542c-560b-bc8f-0fbe2b8bad7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8uv^{3} + 8u^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193976} {:answer/id #uuid "5ad24b67-d3ee-5cf3-9c87-49b1335fbe0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8uv^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193977} {:answer/id #uuid "6377b499-7d79-55e4-8846-6c9884bf45b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv^{3} + 4u^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12cb63f6-04da-555f-b2ff-3767b04d83b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193975} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a445eba-94eb-5e71-9f27-e1e0696f19ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193973}] :question/id #uuid "9fcf8673-a62b-588a-8020-ca78007689b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160840" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u, v)$, where\n\n$F(x, y, z) = ⟨2x + y, 2z, y + z⟩, r(u, v) = ⟨ - u^{2}, 2u^{2} - v^{2}, v^{2}⟩, (u, v) ∈ D⊂R^{2}$.\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$∬_(S)F \\cdot dS = ∬_(D)AAAAAAAdA$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} = ⟨8uv, 4uv, 4uv⟩$.*"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "956510e3-0ede-564b-a4f8-7f3698f007f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193980} {:answer/id #uuid "cd73118b-cac4-5f69-a0de-54bbfa2a44a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193981} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab3018e-5d19-59b1-a01c-c67ddcca9c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193982} {:answer/id #uuid "366f8bbe-0903-53e7-93da-9d71aab6f2fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193983} {:answer/id #uuid "78522f09-5858-5e3d-b17a-1cd32ae40b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "956510e3-0ede-564b-a4f8-7f3698f007f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193980} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc620df2-8885-5b7a-8f11-c8d0842232eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193979}] :question/id #uuid "69fe42a1-24c6-5f53-90f3-883e2fa5e193" :question/math-academy-id "q-160845" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$∬_(S)⟨3x + y + z, \\frac{y}{2} - 2,-3x - z⟩ \\cdot dS$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$r(u, v) = ⟨u - 1, 2v, 2 - 3u - 2v⟩$\n\nfor $-1 \\le u \\le 1$ and $0 \\le v \\le 3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198519 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abb611fa-739f-583c-a2ea-e0822cdfcd03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194016} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4a9a67-3b47-5c59-bd22-6a5d8be8e186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194017} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8c84ae-9834-5e26-898c-a0a5cddaa6a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194018} {:answer/id #uuid "ded35ada-3577-58d8-be4d-f436da7fb349" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194019} {:answer/id #uuid "13ad414e-c611-536a-b4a7-a5f624ac5dcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae4a9a67-3b47-5c59-bd22-6a5d8be8e186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194017} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e1759a5-2eaa-5374-85aa-575bbdf9ae30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194015}] :question/id #uuid "e6b5a3a2-513f-5721-bf54-260cfc8a8f5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-160886" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$∬_(S)⟨2x, \\frac{xz}{3} - 2y, 2z⟩ \\cdot dS$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$r(u, v) = ⟨2u - 1, uv, 3v⟩$\n\nover the domain $D = {(u, v): 0 \\le u \\le 1,-1 \\le v \\le 2}$.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} = ⟨3v,-6, 2u⟩$.*"}]}
